WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
Laurie Myers was born in 1961 as the youngest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.280
of three children after her&nbsp;
siblings Judith and Michael.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.680
When Laurie was just two&nbsp;
years old on October 31st,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.320
1963, Mr. and Mrs. Myers went out for the&nbsp;
evening and Judith, 15-years old at the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:15.600
was spending the night with her boyfriend.&nbsp;
Michael was left in the care of an older woman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.960
named Mrs. Blankenship on their street.&nbsp;
We don’t know exactly where Laurie was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:22.800
but I would assume that she was also left&nbsp;
with Mrs. Blankenship, but given her age, was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:28.160
probably already in bed when Michael snuck out,&nbsp;
grabbed a knife and stuck it into Judith 9 times.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.440
To learn how Laurie’s suppressed&nbsp;
childhood memories may have come back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.160
to save her in the end, that's&nbsp;
a subversion of expectations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:38.593
stick around to the end of this video.&nbsp;
This video is sponsored by Audible.

00:00:38.593 --> 00:00:43.831
(metal intro)

00:00:43.831 --> 00:00:50.080
Welcome to Horror Historyyyyyy. In today’s lesson,&nbsp;
I am analyzing an innocent teenage girl whose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:54.480
biological sibling becomes the most renowned&nbsp;
killer to ever pick up a knife. There are many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.022
versions of this character because there are many&nbsp;
alternate timelines in the Halloween story. &nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.022 --> 00:01:02.640
Most Lauries represent different scenarios branching&nbsp;
off of Halloween night in 1978 -- the events of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:06.400
the original Halloween movie. If you’ve seen&nbsp;
me cover other Halloween franchise characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:09.440
you already know about the Halloween&nbsp;
Express, the train map that I use as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:12.880
an analogy for the Halloween timeline.&nbsp;
In this video, I’ll be analyzing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.640
original timeline where Laurie is played by&nbsp;
Jaime Lee Curtis while she was in her 20s.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:20.320
There may be other videos where we ride the&nbsp;
Halloween Express down alternate routes. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:25.205
for now, let’s take a look at Laurie Strode’s&nbsp;
first appearance in the Halloween franchise.

00:01:25.205 --> 00:01:29.605
(spooky music)

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:33.680
What would you do if the boogeyman&nbsp;
haunting your town was your brother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.120
stalking your every move? Would you&nbsp;
hide under your cover? Would you run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:41.200
away to parts unknown? Would you say,&nbsp;
“Ehh, at least he doesn’t talk a lot.”

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.280
Laurie lost her sister without ever really&nbsp;
knowing her at 2 years old. In a way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:49.200
she lost her brother too, because he was deemed&nbsp;
mentally unfit for society and placed in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.120
sanitarium. It would seem Laurie was taken to visit him at some point. I say this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:56.560
because she later recalls a memory of what&nbsp;
appears to be Michael at the sanitarium,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.040
but for now, this memory is essentially buried.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:03.360
A couple years later, in 1965, her parents&nbsp;
were killed in a car accident and Laurie was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:07.200
placed in the foster care system. Soon after&nbsp;
she was adopted by the Strode family, where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:11.600
her new father figure was a realtor. Being the&nbsp;
last remaining survivor of a pair of tragedies…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.440
outside of her now institutionalized brother…&nbsp;
got the attention of the governor of Illinois,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:19.360
who realized she was still young enough to&nbsp;
maybe have a normal life. He saw to it that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.520
her name was changed and her file was sealed&nbsp;
so no one could connect her with Michael.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.800
For some time, it seemed to have worked.&nbsp;
Laurie has completely forgotten about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.200
her early life and is living&nbsp;
as if it has never happened.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.160
Her foster-parents don’t give her&nbsp;
any information about her youth.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.764
- [Young Laurie] Why won’t you&nbsp;ever tell me anything?

00:02:34.764 --> 00:02:38.080
- [Mrs. Strode] I told you, I’m not your mother.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:43.200
– [Zac] Did these memories fade as all early memories&nbsp;
do, or were they repressed for her own protection?

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.960
We first meet Laurie Strode in her teenage&nbsp;
years, as a kind-hearted student focusing on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:50.720
her grades and her work as a babysitter more&nbsp;
than her social life. Unlike her friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:53.600
she is more of an introvert, though&nbsp;
her babysitting does make her a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:57.360
of contacts in the Haddonfield community&nbsp;
like Doyles with their son Tommy, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.200
Carruthers where she babysits a young Rachel.&nbsp;
She seems to have a connection with these kids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.040
almost like she is so innocent that she prefers&nbsp;
their company to the kids that are her own age.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:08.880
- [Annie] It's tragic. You never&nbsp;
go out. You must have a small&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:13.040
fortune stashed from baby-sitting so much.
- [Laurie] The guys think I'm too smart.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:16.400
– This aspect of her character would&nbsp;
potentially play a role in her survival.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.720
On the morning of Halloween in 1978,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:22.320
Mr. Strode asks her to drop off a key at a&nbsp;
house that he’s selling, which happens to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.240
the Myers house, the same house that fifteen&nbsp;
years before she would have called her home.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:30.320
I think his confidence to send her there on a&nbsp;
casual errand speaks volumes to how everybody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:34.880
felt she had fully recovered. She seems as&nbsp;
unafraid of this house as anyone in Haddonfield.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:38.160
While in class that afternoon, Laurie&nbsp;
seems bored and stares out the window,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.560
but what she finds is more disturbing than&nbsp;
she probably was expecting. Staring back at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:46.880
her across the street is a man with a white&nbsp;
mask and brown car. The teacher distracts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:50.720
her with a question and by the time she looks&nbsp;
back across the street, the man has vanished.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:55.440
Laurie looks confused, perhaps wondering if&nbsp;
her imagination was playing a Halloween trick.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.720
While walking home with her friends that&nbsp;
afternoon, Laurie spots the brown car again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:03.200
now driving up behind them. Her friends think it’s&nbsp;
a guy from their school but Laurie is not so sure.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:07.200
Further ahead, she sees the man disappear behind&nbsp;
some hedges. Her friend Annie investigates, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:10.558
he’s gone before she gets there. Annie believes&nbsp;
that it’s a boy that has a crush on Laurie.

00:04:10.558 --> 00:04:14.960
– Poor Laurie... Looks like you scared another one away.

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:16.640
– Wait, she’s done this before?

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:20.720
Upon getting home, she notices the masked man&nbsp;
standing in her neighbor’s yard just staring at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:24.880
her from behind the clothesline. He mysteriously&nbsp;
vanishes once again. We can see she’s getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:28.480
pretty freaked out by these encounters.&nbsp;
Meanwhile, most of the other high schoolers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:32.800
in Haddonfield are freaking over something else:&nbsp;
the Homecoming dance taking place the next night.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.920
Laurie and Annie discuss it on the way to&nbsp;
their babysitting jobs, and Laurie admits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:39.920
she’s interested in a classmate named Ben Tramer,&nbsp;
but doesn’t feel she has the courage to ask him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:44.000
out. And can you blame her? Ben would literally&nbsp;
become the hottest guy in town that evening.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.360
(tires screeching)
(explosion)

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:48.960
Later that night, while she’s babysitting&nbsp;
Tommy Doyle, Annie shows up and drops off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:52.480
Lindsey Wallace, the child she had been&nbsp;
babysitting, if you want to call it that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:56.320
across the street. There was an unspoken agreement&nbsp;
between the two friends, so that Annie could have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.320 --> 00:05:01.200
some alone time with her boyfriend Paul. This&nbsp;
was the last time Annie was ever seen...alive.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.667
There’s a clear split in priorities when&nbsp;
it comes to Laurie and her friends. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.667 --> 00:05:08.720
are obsessed with hooking up, even if it means&nbsp;
letting their grades, and responsibilities slip,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:12.480
while Laurie makes an effort to do everything&nbsp;
right. She does her homework and she plans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:15.840
out activities for the kids she watches.&nbsp;
She even kind of looks after her friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.160
as we would see later on. For these reasons, when&nbsp;
something isn’t right, Laurie is going to notice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:24.400
it before Annie or Lynda might have. And&nbsp;
that might just be what keeps her alive.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:27.360
Throughout the evening, Tommy keeps&nbsp;
asking Laurie about the boogeyman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:31.440
a legend told to him by his fellow classmates&nbsp;
to try to scare him. She dismisses his concerns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:34.560
though, probably having heard the same&nbsp;
stories when she was in elementary school.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:38.400
After putting the kids to bed, she receives a&nbsp;
weird phone call from her friend Lynda who was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.000
also at the Wallace’s across the street.&nbsp;
What she heard on the other line at first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.000
seemed like cries of passion, but the more&nbsp;
she hears, the more concerned she becomes.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.640
She goes to check on the kids and&nbsp;
they are fast asleep which gives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.520
her time to head across the street to&nbsp;
see what’s up. No one answers the door,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:54.560
but she goes around back and&nbsp;
finds the back door left ajar.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.560
She searches the seemingly empty house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.560 --> 00:06:00.240
but no amount of urban legends could have&nbsp;
prepared her for what she would find.

00:06:01.177 --> 00:06:03.177
(door creaking)

00:06:03.359 --> 00:06:05.359
(cinematic impact)

