00:07:07.201 --> 00:07:10.109
(dark music)

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:14.960
In a bedroom upstairs her friend Annie&nbsp;
is arranged under the tombstone of Judith&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:18.880
Myers. Soonafter, she comes across&nbsp;
the remains of Lynda and Bob as well.

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:22.560
Stricken and emotionally shattered by what&nbsp;
she just found, Laurie runs out of the room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:26.160
to find her worst nightmare waiting for&nbsp;
her. Michael stabs in her direction with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:29.760
kitchen knife and in her terror, she falls&nbsp;
over the railing onto the stairs below.

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:33.200
She hobbles as fast as she can to get out of the&nbsp;
house and tries to get help from the neighbors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.280
who probably assume she’s&nbsp;
playing a Halloween trick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:38.800
and shut her out. It also didn’t help that&nbsp;
she left the door locked without the keys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:42.110
and she had to chuck a flower pot at the&nbsp;
window to wake up Tommy up to let her in.

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:46.160
Mmmmaybe it’s a good thing Michael Myers chose&nbsp;
to carve up Haddonfield that night. It would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:50.000
not have been a look if Tommy’s parents came&nbsp;
home to find Laurie locked out of the house&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:54.640
she’s supposed to be watching, and Tommy sleeping&nbsp;
upstairs in a bed with some girl on their block.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:58.000
Laurie sends Tommy back upstairs, turns out&nbsp;
the lights, and tries to contact someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.160
to help, but finds the phone lines have been cut.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:04.480
Panic sets in when she realizes one of the&nbsp;
downstairs windows has been left open. I don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:08.160
think she gets enough credit for what she does&nbsp;
next. While pretending to plead for her life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:12.080
she also stealthily arms herself with the&nbsp;
best weapon in the room, her knitting needle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:15.120
When Michael nearly impales her again,&nbsp;
after popping out from behind the couch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:17.600
she takes a swing of her own,&nbsp;
sticking him in the neck with it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:21.600
Not yet knowing who or what her attacker is,&nbsp;
she actually believes that this killed him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:25.360
which actually makes her behaviour even more&nbsp;
impressive. I think most people would be a mess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:29.040
if they believed they just murdered someone, and&nbsp;
although she’s clearly shaken by the encounter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:33.360
she keeps her head together enough to remember&nbsp;
her main priority: protecting Tommy and Lindsey.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:37.440
To her shock and terror Michael is&nbsp;
alive and now closing in on them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:41.360
but even under this unimaginable amount of&nbsp;
panic, she still does everything right, as she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:44.000
orders the kids to hide themselves in&nbsp;
a closet as she goes to the bedroom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:48.160
and opens the patio door before taking cover&nbsp;
another closet. I think she does this to make it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:52.240
look like she’d climbed out onto the roof for&nbsp;
help, it’s a nice idea, but it doesn’t work.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:55.680
When Michael finds Laurie, she showcases&nbsp;
her resourcefulness by poking him in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:59.360
eye with a wire hanger, causing him to drop&nbsp;
his knife. I honestly can’t believe that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:03.200
works. Every time I watch it, it’s just like&nbsp;
how does she get the thing to stay straight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:07.040
enough to go into his eye? I maybe would have&nbsp;
gone for one of those wooden shades instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:09.040
but what can I say? It worked out for her.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:10.880
She retrieves Tommy and Lindsey from their hiding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:12.880
place and tells them to run down the block for help.

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:14.400
– Go do as I say.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:15.920
– She may be shy with her school crush,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:19.840
but she's certainly capable of becoming&nbsp;
authoritative when the occasion calls for it.

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:24.240
However, this puts her in a bad position because&nbsp;
she's caught off guard by Michael yet again. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:28.400
strangles her with his bare hands, and in an&nbsp;
act of desperation, she rips off his mask.

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:32.080
I'm not going to try to analyze this as a&nbsp;
strategic move by Laurie because I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:35.760
it's pretty clear that it was just instinct. I&nbsp;
think a lot of horror fans like to paint&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:39.600
her as this rarity, like she's one of the&nbsp;
smart ones. But between forgetting her keys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:42.960
leaving the knife behind and turning her back&nbsp;
to the guy that's trying to slice her up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:46.240
this probably isn't a test that she'd be&nbsp;
posting up on her fridge. She's passing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:49.600
but not with flying colors, and not&nbsp;
without a little bit of luck as well.

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:53.600
And this was her luckiest moment, because when&nbsp;
she pulls off Michael's mask, a gunshot rings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:57.360
out from the darkness and a man in a trench&nbsp;
coat, who we know as Dr. Samuel Loomis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:01.520
shoots Michael several times knocking him&nbsp;
off of the balcony and saving Laurie's life.

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:05.520
He tells her that that was, in fact, the&nbsp;
boogeyman and she breaks down into tears.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:09.040
Between the cuts she received from Michael&nbsp;
and her physical and mental exhaustion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:12.240
from that night’s events, they actually&nbsp;
have to take her away on a stretcher and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:15.280
in the ambo, she’s very adamant&nbsp;
about not being put to sleep.

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:17.120
– Don’t let them put me to sleep.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:21.520
– After arriving at Haddonfield Memorial Hospital,&nbsp;
she is again adamant with the Dr. that she not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:26.080
be sedated. What is the reasoning for this? I&nbsp;
don’t think Laurie herself fully understands.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:29.680
I think the desire not to go to sleep&nbsp;
is coming from her subconscious mind.

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:33.280
Earlier, I discussed how she was able to suppress&nbsp;
her childhood memories about what happened to her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:37.840
family in the mid 1960s. This was basically done&nbsp;
as a defense mechanism so that she could go back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:41.920
to living a semi-normal life without constantly&nbsp;
being reminded of those painful memories. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:45.840
didn’t do this on purpose, it was just her&nbsp;
subconscious brain trying to protect her.

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:50.240
I should note that in real life, the idea of&nbsp;
repressed memories, or as the American Psychiatric&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:54.800
Association puts it: “dissociative amnesia”&nbsp;
is not commonly accepted as a real phenomenon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:59.120
but since we’re in the world of Halloween and not&nbsp;
the real world, I’m willing to look past that.

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:02.640
So Laurie didn’t want to go to sleep because&nbsp;
those harmful memories had to go somewhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.680
and some part of her realized that&nbsp;
it was her dreams where the truth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:09.120
was hidden. Dr. Mixter ignores her&nbsp;
request however, and sedates her.

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:12.415
When she came to, she would receive some horrifying information, 

00:11:12.415 --> 00:11:15.749
making her experiences to that point seem that much scarier.

00:11:16.451 --> 00:11:18.451
(big impact)

00:11:21.266 --> 00:11:23.266
(mysterious music)

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:29.920
Laurie wakes up to a hospital employee named Jimmy who&nbsp;
fills her in on who her mysterious attacker was.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:33.200
She recognizes the name in relation to the&nbsp;
Myers house, but does not understand why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:37.120
Michael has chosen her to hunt. Jimmy is kicked&nbsp;
out by the charge nurse who tells Laurie that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:40.560
they’re having trouble getting in contact with&nbsp;
her parents because the phones are not working.

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:44.320
As the clock creeps into the earliest part of&nbsp;
November, Laurie eventually succumbs to her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:48.560
exhaustion and falls asleep. Sure enough, she&nbsp;
dreams of some creepy memories from her youth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:52.640
including her foster-mother refusing to tell her&nbsp;
about her past and a strange, yet familiar boy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:56.000
looking out a window. I think her brain&nbsp;
is slowly putting together the pieces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.000 --> 00:12:00.320
about who this forgotten boy is, because her&nbsp;
experience that evening, in particular, the moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:04.480
where she tore off Michael’s mask, is slowly&nbsp;
kicking that part of her brain back into gear.

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:08.720
On some level, she seems terrified by this, and&nbsp;
not wanting to dig into her past any further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:11.280
she does everything she can to&nbsp;
stay awake, eventually resulting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:14.880
in her just sleeping with her eyes wide&nbsp;
open which concerns the medical staff.

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:18.720
Eventually, Laurie wakes up. I’m guessing it’s&nbsp;
right here while this nurse is investigating a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:22.560
disturbance outside. Between that, and the&nbsp;
cut phone lines, I guess she realized that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:26.880
something was up at this hospital, and that&nbsp;
maybe she hadn’t evaded the danger quite yet.

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:30.640
She sets up a decoy in her bed using pillows&nbsp;
-- and can we just pause for a second?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:34.880
Why is this a movie trope? I talked about this&nbsp;
exact same trap when I covered Andy Barclay from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:39.120
Child’s Play. I guess the idea is that the bad&nbsp;
guy will come in, see this lump under the bed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:43.120
and then go attack that instead of immediately&nbsp;
going to find his victim. But what does that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:47.040
save you, like 2 seconds? You’re better off&nbsp;
not taking the time to set up the decoy.

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:50.640
Anyway, this leads to her wandering the halls&nbsp;
in a dazed state, trying to get her hands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:54.560
on a working phone to no avail. She collapses&nbsp;
in a ball on the floor, and we’re just forced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:58.560
to sit there for 22 seconds watching her&nbsp;
fall asleep, this goes on way too long.

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:01.680
Eventually, Laurie gets back to her feet,&nbsp;
still in a bit of a drugged up state,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:04.720
and the nurse tries to come get her,&nbsp;
and Laurie turns just in time to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:08.800
Michael Myers stab her in the back with&nbsp;
a scalpel. And this is Laurie’s reaction.

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:12.960
She hobbles away in the slowest chase ever.&nbsp;
Laurie is slowed by her injuries and sedatives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:18.480
and Michael is just a slow walker, that’s how he&nbsp;
is. She ends up barely, and I mean, barely evading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:22.960
him behind a closing elevator door. Some people&nbsp;
really will do anything to avoid using the stairs.

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:26.000
Anyway, Laurie hides in random car,&nbsp;
which turns out to be Jimmy’s car,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:29.840
but it won’t start because the fuel line has&nbsp;
been cut, and he also collapses onto the horn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:33.520
drawing Michael’s attention back to them.&nbsp;
She does, however, see a possible chance to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:37.280
get to safety when, Dr. Loomis pulls up with&nbsp;
a state marshal. She tries calling out for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:40.880
help but when she screams, she’s not able to&nbsp;
produce enough sound to get their attention.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:43.760
When I did the Horror History episode&nbsp;
on Laurie’s daughter, Jamie Lloyd,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:47.680
I talked about how she, at one point, suffered&nbsp;
from a condition known as selective mutism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:49.920
rendering her unable to speak. As it turns out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:54.000
this condition can be brought on by a number&nbsp;
of factors, and genetic makeup is one of them.

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:57.760
Laurie’s inability to speak only lasts a few&nbsp;
moments, but given that her brother Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.760 --> 00:14:02.320
stopped speaking after his traumatic event on Halloween&nbsp;
and her eventual daughter Jamie lost her voice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:05.920
for a year under similar circumstances, that&nbsp;
could be the reason that she’s not able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:10.000
call for help. It also fits in with the theme of&nbsp;
dreams and nightmares present in Halloween II,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.800
which I talk more about in this&nbsp;
episode of Things You Missed.

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:16.400
Laurie is chased by Michael again, and&nbsp;
Dr. Loomis eventually lets her in just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:18.400
before Michael comes crashing through the door.

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:22.240
Loomis shoots him down, but at this point,&nbsp;
his ability rise back up and give chase is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:25.440
no surprise to either of them. They&nbsp;
find shelter in an empty operating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:28.735
room. Loomis tries handing Laurie his&nbsp;
gun but she is hesitant to take it.

00:14:29.117 --> 00:14:30.288
– [Loomis] C’mon, c’mon, c’mon.&nbsp;

00:14:30.288 --> 00:14:32.000
– No.
– Take it.

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:34.240
– You would think in a life or&nbsp;
death situation like this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:37.920
she would want to arm herself. We’ve already&nbsp;
seen she has no problem fighting back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:40.960
based on her actions earlier that&nbsp;
night, so what’s going on here?

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:43.120
This could go back to the&nbsp;
innocence of her character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:47.280
but it may also be the realization dawning&nbsp;
on her that the Michael Myers before her is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:51.280
the very same boy seen staring out the&nbsp;
window in her dreams, her own brother.

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:54.880
Michael stabs Loomis and turns his attention&nbsp;
to Laurie, who comes to her senses and shoots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:58.960
him in the face -- temporarily blinding him.&nbsp;
While he is hopelessly slashing at the air,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:02.320
she sees Dr. Loomis opening the&nbsp;
compressed gas canisters in the room.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:05.280
Realizing that he’s being lured&nbsp;
away by the sound, she follows suit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:08.160
which makes it harder for him to track&nbsp;
them using the sound of their movements.

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:11.200
After receiving the word from Loomis, she&nbsp;
runs out of the room and down the hall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:14.960
when she feels the room she left behind&nbsp;
explode and knock her off of her feet.

00:15:15.396 --> 00:15:17.396
(explosion)

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:23.440
When Laurie turns to look at the blaze, to&nbsp;
her absolute horror, a burning figure is walking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:27.920
towards her. Laurie doesn’t even move when she&nbsp;
sees this, almost as if she’s given up the fight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:32.080
If stabbing him, poking his eye out, shooting&nbsp;
him 13 times, and blowing him up was not enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:36.880
to stop him, maybe Michael just could not&nbsp;
be defeated. However, that would be as far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:40.800
as he would go, as Laurie watches him&nbsp;
collapse face first for the final time.

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:44.740
Emergency services show up at the scene that&nbsp;
morning to put out the fire and rescue her. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.740 --> 00:15:48.640
is wheeled out of the hospital to yet another&nbsp;
ambulance. News crews try to speak with her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:52.640
but she basically gives them the Marshawn Lynch&nbsp;
treatment, and refuses to speak with the media.

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:55.360
She asks to sit in the front,&nbsp;
perhaps not wanting to relive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:57.280
any part of the journey she had just been through.

00:15:57.280 --> 00:16:00.880
All in all, Laurie Strode was traumatized&nbsp;
by that evening's events. She discovered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:04.400
the deaths of three of her friends, nearly&nbsp;
lost her own life, witnessed the murder of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:09.120
a nurse and played a part in an explosion that&nbsp;
all but killed two people. I’m sure any thoughts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:13.280
of attending that Homecoming dance were already out&nbsp;
the window at this point, as she would probably be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:17.360
spending the next 24 hours in another hospital,&nbsp;
but she would later discover that Ben Tramer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:17.360 --> 00:16:21.600
the boy she was interested in attending the dance&nbsp;
with, had also been killed that Halloween night.

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:25.360
Maybe it is because Laurie has dealt with&nbsp;
tragedy her entire life, but she actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:29.360
moves on pretty quickly from Ben Tramer, and&nbsp;
ends up getting together with a man named Mr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:33.600
Lloyd almost immediately. There is a popular&nbsp;
fan theory that Mr. Lloyd is actually Jimmy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:36.320
because we never learn his last name,&nbsp;
he seems to be interested in her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:38.880
and the two share a bond in having&nbsp;
gone through the most terrifying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:42.880
night ever together, but I can neither&nbsp;
confirm or deny that he is Mr Lloyd.

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:46.240
It’s only a little over a year later that&nbsp;
she becomes pregnant with their child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:51.280
and in either late 1980 or early 1981, she&nbsp;
gives birth to a daughter named Jamie. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:54.480
think her name goes against the whole “Jimmy&nbsp;
is Mr. Lloyd” theory, just because it would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:57.760
be confusing having a household&nbsp;
consisting of Jimmy and Jamie.

00:16:57.760 --> 00:17:01.520
But if that is the case, it would not have been&nbsp;
a problem for very long, because in November&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:06.800
of 1987, Laurie and Jamie’s father get into a&nbsp;
fatal car accident, just like Laurie’s parents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:10.640
before her. We don’t know much about those&nbsp;
final years leading up to Laurie’s death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:10.640 --> 00:17:14.800
but it at least seems as if her and Jamie’s father&nbsp;
had a good relationship with their daughter.

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:16.720
– I know you miss your parents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:19.920
it hasn’t been that long.
– It’s been 11 months.

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:23.280
– [Zac] Jamie is left with a shoebox containing&nbsp;
photos of her mom when she was younger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:25.360
and curiously, a photo of Michael as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:29.120
perhaps suggesting that Laurie did&nbsp;
teach her about her dark family history.

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:32.480
If you want to see me speculate further about&nbsp;
Laurie and Jamie’s limited time together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:35.840
you’ll want to watch Jamie’s episode of Horror&nbsp;
History, which you can find by clicking that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:40.160
video on the left. Remember to subscribe&nbsp;
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:46.875
RING the deathbell for ALL notifications, and I’ll&nbsp;
see you in the next one. Assuming we both survive.

00:17:47.624 --> 00:17:49.624
(rock music)

